course: dictionary
lesson: 4769
title: Hover: staying still, staying close
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hover is a word that can mean a few different things, so context helps you choose. «A kestrel hovers into the wind with its head perfectly still.» Here hover means it stays in the air in one place, with its wings flapping and its body not moving forward.
explain: Hover can also mean to stand or wait near someone, often nervously. «Please stop hovering near my desk» means the person is close by, maybe waiting for something and unsure what to do. You can tell from the words around it, like nervously or near.
explain: When a number is involved, hover around means to stay close to it. «The temperature hovered around 20 degrees» means it stayed near 20, not exactly 20 and not far away. On a screen, hover means to hold the mouse pointer over something without clicking.
fact: To hover means to stay in the air in one place without moving forward.
fact: Birds, insects and drones can all hover.
fact: Hover around a number means to stay close to that number.
fact: On a computer, to hover means to hold the mouse pointer over something on the screen.
fact: Hover often appears with the words over, around and near, as in «hover over», «hover around» and «hover near».
exercise: «A kestrel can hover over the long grass.» What does hover mean here? | *Stay in the air in one place | Dig a hole in the ground | Fly very fast into a tree | Sing loudly to its friends
exercise: Temperatures «hover around 20 degrees.» What does hover around mean? | Fall to zero and stay there | Turn into ice | *Stay close to 20 | Jump up past 30
exercise: «Please stop hovering near my desk.» What might hovering mean? | Sleeping on the floor | Flying in the air | *Standing close by, waiting nervously | Running a race
test: In «Fish rest by hovering still», what does still mean? | Very cold | Very fast | Drinking water | *Not moving
test: Move the mouse pointer to hover over the picture. What does hover mean on a screen? | Delete it from the screen | Draw a line round it | Click it twice to open it | *Hold the pointer over it, without clicking
exam: Which sentence uses hover to mean stay in the air in one place? | «The price hovered around ten pounds.» | «He hovered over the keyboard all afternoon.» | *«Hummingbirds can hover and fly backwards.» | «She hovered near the door, not sure whether to go in.»
